Fix newFounder/cold_start conflation bug

newFounder (the 'New founders only' dashboard filter) was wired to reuse cold_start
(our data-confidence flag). Once GITHUB_TOKEN fixed rate-limiting and real scoring
started succeeding, cold_start correctly flipped to False (enough evidence to trust
the score) -- which incorrectly hid those exact candidates from the default filtered
view, since newFounder flipped False along with it.

Decoupled: newFounder now reflects actual footprint size (followers/repos/stars,
same thresholds as the original prototype heuristic), independent of scoring
confidence. Added is_low_footprint() for the live-scan path and
is_low_footprint_from_signals() for the Memory-reload path. coldStart is now also
exposed separately on the candidate payload rather than overloading newFounder.
